 ## Background
-DIF-Gaussian was introduced by the xmed-lab group [S1, unofficial]. It is used for CBCT volume reconstruction [S1, unofficial]. The method builds on the principles of feed-forward generalizable reconstruction, extending them by incorporating Gaussian splatting for feature interpolation [Parent, S1, unofficial].
